WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.112
Can Trinzic run an agency's DDI alone
once workloads move to the clouds?

2
00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:07.313
On its own, it can see into them,

3
00:00:07.313 --> 00:00:13.000
discovering networks and importing zones
one way, but it can't own cloud DNS.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.368
There are three ways to
extend it, and they combine:

5
00:00:16.368 --> 00:00:19.654
virtual appliances in each
cloud, Universal DDI,

6
00:00:19.654 --> 00:00:23.761
which is the only Infoblox path
that writes back to cloud DNS,

7
00:00:23.761 --> 00:00:28.525
or native cloud resolvers wired to
the Grid with forwarding both ways.

8
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:31.476
The design guidance is
this: mostly on premises,

9
00:00:31.476 --> 00:00:35.864
use native resolvers with forwarding;
hybrid, add virtual appliances;

10
00:00:35.864 --> 00:00:41.084
multi-cloud at Moderate, add Universal DDI
for workloads in the commercial regions,

11
00:00:41.084 --> 00:00:45.321
after confirming which features
the government edition supports;

12
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:48.650
and for FedRAMP High, don't
depend on the Moderate SaaS.

13
00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:51.310
The Trinzic explainer
has the full reasoning.
